# Private, machine-specific, or otherwise never-tracked material.
# `local/` holds absolute paths and private sibling names — it must never enter history.
local/

node_modules/

# Scratch: fixtures, probes, dumps. Never OS temp (see the doctrine's no-tmp rule).
_fixtures/

*.log
.DS_Store

# The canon is staged into the CLI package at pack time (tools/stage-package.mjs);
# the tracked copy is canon/ at the root.
src/Daoris.Cli/canon/
src/Daoris.Cli/LICENSE
src/Daoris.Cli/README.md

# .NET build output.
#
# NOT a blanket `bin/`: `src/Daoris.Cli/bin` is the CLI's published entry point — the file npm's
# `bin` field points at — and a global rule would untrack the one thing the package cannot ship
# without. Every .NET tree is listed instead, and adding a new one means adding a line here.
#
# The previous version listed the trees that existed when it was written, so the devkit's 397 build
# artefacts were staged the first time it was built. Scoping by `src/*/` rather than by name would
# be tidier and would also catch `src/Daoris.Cli/bin`, which is exactly the file it must not catch.
src/Daoris.Service/**/bin/
src/Daoris.Service/**/obj/
src/Daoris.Devkit/**/bin/
src/Daoris.Devkit/**/obj/

# The web UI's build output. `Daoris.Web` builds INTO the HTTP host on purpose, so the API and the page
# share one origin — which is what makes CORS unnecessary in a real deployment and lets the desktop
# shell host exactly the same bytes. The source is `src/Daoris.Web`; this is what vite made of it.
src/Daoris.Service/Daoris.Service.Http/wwwroot/
